  _globals['_BILLINGSERVICE'].methods_by_name['GetBillingConfig']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_BILLINGSERVICE'].methods_by_name['GetBillingConfig']._serialized_options = b'\222A\313\003\n\007Billing\022\031Get billing configuration\032\321\002Returns configuration needed to bootstrap client-side billing integrations, such as the Stripe publishable key used to initialize Stripe.js before mounting an embedded Checkout session. This is a single deployment-wide value, not scoped to the workspace\'s enrolment state, so it is available even before AddPaymentMethod has been called.JQ\n\003200\022J\n\025Billing configuration\0221\n/\032-.scalekit.v1.billing.GetBillingConfigResponse\202\265\030\002\030D\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\002\030\022\026/api/v1/billing:config'
  _globals['_BILLINGSERVICE'].methods_by_name['GetBillingCatalog']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_BILLINGSERVICE'].methods_by_name['GetBillingCatalog']._serialized_options = b'\222A\241\004\n\007Billing\022\027Get the billing catalog\032\342\002Returns the product lines, plans and prices to render a pricing or plan page. Resolves the catalog version the caller should see: an explicitly requested version, else the version this workspace is pinned to, else the region\'s current version. A workspace keeps seeing its own pinned version\'s allowances after new customers have moved on to a later one.Ja\n\003200\022Z\n$The catalog for the resolved version\0222\n0\032..scalekit.v1.billing.GetBillingCatalogResponseJ5\n\003404\022.\n,The requested catalog version does not exist\202\265\030\020\n\014billing:read\030D\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\002\031\022\027/api/v1/billing/catalog'
  _globals['_BILLINGSERVICE'].methods_by_name['GetBillingAccount']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_BILLINGSERVICE'].methods_by_name['GetBillingAccount']._serialized_options = b'\222A\271\005\n\007Billing\022!Get the workspace billing account\032\256\004Returns the workspace\'s billing state regardless of billing generation: lifecycle status, whether a payment method has been captured, payment health, billing identifiers, and the pinned catalog version. A workspace with no billing artifacts yet reports a pending account with no card \342\200\224 that is data, not an error. Card capture is asynchronous \342\200\224 AddPaymentMethod returns a Checkout session for the client to mount, and the card is only verified when Stripe reports the session complete \342\200\224 so poll this to know when production environments can be created.JZ\n\003200\022S\n\035The workspace\'s billing state\0222\n0\032..scalekit.v1.billing.GetBillingAccountResponse\202\265\030\020\n\014billing:read\030D\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\002\031\022\027/api/v1/billing/account'
  _globals['_BILLINGSERVICE'].methods_by_name['AddPaymentMethod']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_BILLINGSERVICE'].methods_by_name['AddPaymentMethod']._serialized_options = b'\222A\254\007\n\007Billing\022\024Add a payment method\032\274\005Starts Stripe Checkout in setup mode to capture a payment method, enrolling the workspace in billing when it is not already. No charge is made \342\200\224 setup mode stores a card for later use. Use this before creating a production environment, which requires a verified payment method. The session is always embedded: mount it in your own page with Stripe.js EmbeddedCheckout using the returned client_secret and the publishable key from GetBillingConfig. The account becomes active once the card is verified via the checkout completion webhook, so poll GetBillingAccount to learn when that has happened. Idempotent \342\200\224 a workspace that already has a payment method gets no new session unless force is set.J\226\001\n\003200\022\216\001\nYIncludes the client secret for mounting embedded Checkout, and the billing account status\0221\n/\032-.scalekit.v1.billing.AddPaymentMethodResponseJ3\n\003400\022,\n*Billing is not enabled for this deployment\202\265\030\021\n\rbilling:write\030D\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\002\'\"\"/api/v1/billing:add-payment-method:\001*'
  _globals['_BILLINGSERVICE'].methods_by_name['ListPaymentMethods']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_BILLINGSERVICE'].methods_by_name['ListPaymentMethods']._serialized_options = b'\222A\337\006\n\007Billing\022$List the workspace\'s payment methods\032\213\004Lists the payment methods saved for the workspace, newest first, with the card brand, last four digits and expiry, never the full card number. The method invoices and paid plan changes charge is marked as the default; when none is set, the newest usable card is made the default first. Each method reports whether it can still be charged, so a client knows which ones may become the default. Use AddPaymentMethod with force to add a card, SetDefaultPaymentMethod to switch the default and RemovePaymentMethod to delete one.Jw\n\003200\022p\n9The workspace\'s payment methods; empty when none is saved\0223\n1\032/.scalekit.v1.billing.ListPaymentMethodsResponseJ\246\001\n\003400\022\236\001\n\233\001Billing is not enabled for this deployment, or the workspace is not billed through Metronome (legacy workspaces manage cards in the Stripe customer portal)\202\265\030\020\n\014billing:read\030D\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\002!\022\037/api/v1/billing/payment-methods'
  _globals['_BILLINGSERVICE'].methods_by_name['SetDefaultPaymentMethod']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_BILLINGSERVICE'].methods_by_name['SetDefaultPaymentMethod']._serialized_options = b'\222A\206\006\n\007Billing\022\036Set the default payment method\032\212\003Makes a saved payment method the one future invoices and paid plan changes charge. Use this to switch back to a card added earlier without entering it again. Only a method saved for this workspace is accepted, and only one that can still be charged: an expired card, or one that failed the bank\'s checks when it was saved, is refused. Setting the current default again succeeds without changes.Jh\n\003200\022a\n%The payment method is now the default\0228\n6\0324.scalekit.v1.billing.SetDefaultPaymentMethodResponseJ\237\001\n\003400\022\227\001\n\224\001The payment method cannot be charged (expired or failed the bank\'s checks), billing is not enabled, or the workspace is not billed through MetronomeJB\n\003404\022;\n9No payment method with this id is saved for the workspace\202\265\030\021\n\rbilling:write\030D\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\002D\"?/api/v1/billing/payment-methods/{payment_method_id}:set-default:\001*'
  _globals['_BILLINGSERVICE'].methods_by_name['RemovePaymentMethod']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_BILLINGSERVICE'].methods_by_name['RemovePaymentMethod']._serialized_options = b'\222A\332\004\n\007Billing\022\027Remove a payment method\032\234\002Deletes a saved payment method from the workspace for good; it cannot be charged again and must be entered again to be reused. The default payment method cannot be removed, so invoices always have a method to charge: make another method the default with SetDefaultPaymentMethod first.J]\n\003200\022V\n\036The payment method was removed\0224\n2\0320.scalekit.v1.billing.RemovePaymentMethodResponseJt\n\003400\022m\nkThe payment method is the default, billing is not enabled, or the workspace is not billed through MetronomeJB\n\003404\022;\n9No payment method with this id is saved for the workspace\202\265\030\021\n\rbilling:write\030D\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\0025*3/api/v1/billing/payment-methods/{payment_method_id}'
  _globals['_BILLINGSERVICE'].methods_by_name['ListEnvironmentBilling']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_BILLINGSERVICE'].methods_by_name['ListEnvironmentBilling']._serialized_options = b'\222A\253\003\n\007Billing\022\030List environment billing\032\241\002Lists every production environment in the workspace with the plan it is on for each product line, standalone add-ons it pays for, add-ons it can still buy, its billing contract, and the catalog version its prices are pinned to. Development environments are not billed and are not returned.Jb\n\003200\022[\n One entry per billed environment\0227\n5\0323.scalekit.v1.billing.ListEnvironmentBillingResponse\202\265\030\020\n\014billing:read\030D\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\002\036\022\034/api/v1/billing/environments'
  _globals['_BILLINGSERVICE'].methods_by_name['UpdateBillingPlan']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_BILLINGSERVICE'].methods_by_name['UpdateBillingPlan']._serialized_options = b'\222A\234\021\n\007Billing\022%Change the current environment\'s plan\032\302\nMoves the CURRENT production environment \342\200\224 the one this request\'s environment context resolves to \342\200\224 to a different plan on one or more product lines. Lines omitted from the request keep their current plan. Prices stay pinned to the workspace\'s catalog version, so a plan change never re-prices the lines it does not touch. A downgrade is applied even when current usage exceeds the new plan\'s allowance. The exceeded-allowance list in the response is reserved for that reporting and is not populated yet, so a caller cannot currently tell from this response what the change constrained. add_ons is the complete set of standalone add-ons after the call. Omit it or send an empty list to cancel every add-on. Resubmit EnvironmentBilling.add_ons when you only want to change the plan. A change that adds recurring cost is first authorized on the workspace\'s default card for the increase; the authorization is released once the change is applied, and the first invoice does the charge. With no usable card, or when the card is declined, the change is refused and nothing is applied. When the bank requires authentication (3-D Secure), the response carries payment_action and the plan is left unchanged: complete the action with Stripe.js, then resend the same request with payment_authorization_id set to payment_action.payment_authorization_id.J\207\002\n\003200\022\377\001\n\310\001The environment\'s plan after the call. When payment_action is set, the change was not applied and the plan returned is the unchanged one. The exceeded-allowance list is reserved and not populated yet.\0222\n0\032..scalekit.v1.billing.UpdateBillingPlanResponseJ\362\002\n\003400\022\352\002\n\347\002Unknown product line or plan; or the change was refused at the payment step and nothing was applied: PAYMENT_METHOD_REQUIRED (no usable card on file), PAYMENT_DECLINED (the card declined the authorization), or PAYMENT_AUTHORIZATION_INVALID (payment_authorization_id is not this environment\'s authorization for this change, or authentication was not completed)J0\n\003404\022)\n\'The environment has no billing contractJt\n\003500\022m\nkThe card could not be checked with the payment provider; nothing was applied and the request can be retried\202\265\030\021\n\rbilling:write\030D\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\002\0312\024/api/v1/billing/plan:\001*'
  _globals['_BILLINGSERVICE'].methods_by_name['GetBillingUsage']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_BILLINGSERVICE'].methods_by_name['GetBillingUsage']._serialized_options = b'\222A\260\004\n\007Billing\0222Get the current environment\'s current-period usage\032\321\001Returns current-period usage against allowance for every metered entitlement on this environment\'s plan. Only meaningful on a Metronome-generation billing account; a Stripe-generation account returns an error.J\177\n\003200\022x\nDOne entry per metered entitlement governed by the environment\'s plan\0220\n.\032,.scalekit.v1.billing.GetBillingUsageResponseJ2\n\003400\022+\n)The workspace has no billing customer yetJh\n\003404\022a\n_The environment has no billing contract, or this account is not on Metronome-generation billing\202\265\030\020\n\014billing:read\030D\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\002\027\022\025/api/v1/billing/usage'
  _globals['_BILLINGSERVICE'].methods_by_name['GetBillingConnectionCounts']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_BILLINGSERVICE'].methods_by_name['GetBillingConnectionCounts']._serialized_options = b'\222A\275\004\n\007Billing\022KGet the current environment\'s live SSO connection and SCIM directory counts\032\371\001Returns the live count of active SSO connections and active SCIM directories in this environment, read from the database. Do not use GetBillingUsage for this: that value is fractional connection-months accrued this period, not a point-in-time count.J\177\n\003200\022x\n9Live connection and directory counts for this environment\022;\n9\0327.scalekit.v1.billing.GetBillingConnectionCountsResponseJh\n\003404\022a\n_The environment has no billing contract, or this account is not on Metronome-generation billing\202\265\030\020\n\014billing:read\030D\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\002#\022!/api/v1/billing/connection-counts'
  _globals['_BILLINGSERVICE'].methods_by_name['GetInvoicesDashboardUrl']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_BILLINGSERVICE'].methods_by_name['GetInvoicesDashboardUrl']._serialized_options = b'\222A\326\005\n\007Billing\022DGet an embeddable invoices dashboard URL for the current environment\032\307\002Returns a short-lived, authenticated URL for Metronome\'s hosted invoices dashboard, scoped to this environment\'s billing contract. Mint a fresh URL per view rather than caching it \342\200\224 the URL itself is a bearer credential. Only meaningful on a Metronome-generation billing account; a Stripe-generation account returns an error.J^\n\003200\022W\n\033An embeddable dashboard URL\0228\n6\0324.scalekit.v1.billing.GetInvoicesDashboardUrlResponseJq\n\003400\022j\nhThe workspace has no billing customer yet, or this environment\'s billing contract is not provisioned yetJh\n\003404\022a\n_The environment has no billing contract, or this account is not on Metronome-generation billing\202\265\030\020\n\014billing:read\030D\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\002$\022\"/api/v1/billing/invoices-dashboard'
  _globals['_BILLINGSERVICE'].methods_by_name['GetSupportWorkspaceBilling']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_BILLINGSERVICE'].methods_by_name['GetSupportWorkspaceBilling']._serialized_options = b'\222A\207\007\n\007Billing\022(Get a customer workspace\'s billing state\032\326\004Returns the billing account and, for every environment of a customer workspace that has a billing contract (production environments; environments without a contract are not listed), its plan, add-ons and negotiated entitlements. Contracts are listed whatever their status. Use it before changing a customer\'s billing on their behalf: each environment carries the etag that UpdateSupportEnvironmentBilling requires. With include_live, also reads each contract from the billing provider and reports where it disagrees with the stored copy. Callable only by members of the Scalekit platform workspace.J\201\001\n\003200\022z\n;The workspace\'s billing account and production environments\022;\n9\0327.scalekit.v1.billing.GetSupportWorkspaceBillingResponseJF\n\003403\022?\n=The caller is not a member of the Scalekit platform workspaceJ-\n\003404\022&\n$The workspace has no billing account\202\265\030\020\n\014billing:read\030D\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\0023\0221/api/v1/billing/support/workspaces/{workspace_id}'
  _globals['_BILLINGSERVICE'].methods_by_name['UpdateSupportEnvironmentBilling']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_BILLINGSERVICE'].methods_by_name['UpdateSupportEnvironmentBilling']._serialized_options = b'\222A\376\013\n\007Billing\0227Change a customer environment\'s billing on their behalf\032\225\006Applies an ordered list of operations to one customer production environment: set a product line\'s plan (negotiated tiers included), add or remove a paid add-on, and set or remove a negotiated entitlement. Items not named keep their current state. All operations are compiled into a single contract edit and applied all-or-nothing. Requires the etag from GetSupportWorkspaceBilling, so a change computed against stale state is refused, and a reason of 10 to 500 characters naming the deal or ticket, which is recorded in the audit event. A negotiated entitlement must be at or above the resulting plan\'s stock terms. With dry_run, validates and returns the resulting state and the exact contract change without writing anything. Callable only by members of the Scalekit platform workspace.J\235\001\n\003200\022\225\001\nQThe resulting (or, for a dry run, would-be) billing state and the contract change\022@\n>\032<.scalekit.v1.billing.UpdateSupportEnvironmentBillingResponseJ\217\002\n\003400\022\207\002\n\204\002The request is invalid: reason missing or not 10 to 500 characters, etag missing, no operations or more than 50, or an operation is invalid (unknown line, tier or entitlement, wrong value kind, a value below the plan\'s stock terms, or contradicting operations)JF\n\003403\022?\n=The caller is not a member of the Scalekit platform workspaceJ0\n\003404\022)\n\'The environment has no billing contractJv\n\003409\022o\nmThe etag no longer matches the environment\'s billing state, or another change on this contract is in progress\202\265\030\021\n\rbilling:write\030D\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\002:25/api/v1/billing/support/environments/{environment_id}:\001*'
  _globals['_BILLINGSERVICE'].methods_by_name['UpdateSupportWorkspaceBillingAccount']._loaded_options = None
  _globals['_BILLINGSERVICE'].methods_by_name['UpdateSupportWorkspaceBillingAccount']._serialized_options = b'\222A\256\007\n\007Billing\0223Change a customer\'s billing account on their behalf\032\220\004Grants or removes the production card exemption for a customer workspace. An exempt workspace can create and use production environments without a payment method on file, for customers who pay by invoice. Removing the exemption restores the verified state when the payments provider has a default payment method for the customer, and clears it otherwise; existing production environments are never removed. With dry_run, returns the resulting account without writing. Callable only by members of the Scalekit platform workspace.J\214\001\n\003200\022\204\001\n;The resulting (or, for a dry run, would-be) billing account\022E\nC\032A.scalekit.v1.billing.UpdateSupportWorkspaceBillingAccountResponseJU\n\003400\022N\nLNo operation was given, or the reason is missing or not 10 to 500 charactersJF\n\003403\022?\n=The caller is not a member of the Scalekit platform workspaceJ-\n\003404\022&\n$The workspace has no billing account\202\265\030\021\n\rbilling:write\030D\372\322\344\223\002\t\022\007PREVIEW\202\323\344\223\002>29/api/v1/billing/support/workspaces/{workspace_id}/account:\001*'
